      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We consider a one-dimensional classical Coulomb gas of N-like charges in a harmonic potential-also known as the one-dimensional one-component plasma. We compute, analytically, the probability distribution of the position x_{max} of the rightmost charge in the limit of large N. We show that the typical fluctuations of x_{max} around its mean are described by a nontrivial scaling function, with asymmetric tails. This distribution is different from the Tracy-Widom distribution of x_{max} for Dyson's log gas. We also compute the large deviation functions of x_{max} explicitly and show that the system exhibits a third-order phase transition, as in the log gas. Our theoretical predictions are verified numerically."},
